    "q-53557": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53557",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Ken's tree has a diameter of $4\\,\\text{ft}.$ What length of chain does Ken need for it to wrap around the tree perfectly?",
      "worked_solution": "The length of the chain needed to wrap around the tree is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=4\\,\\text{ft}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 4=4\\pi \\,\\text{ft}.\n$$",
